+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates caller-supplied tool input against the resolved tool definition before an executor can run.
+
+- A missing required property or a property with the wrong type returns a `ToolResponse` describing the failed constraint, does not invoke the executor, and does not expose the rejected value ([validated by: rejects schema-invalid input without invoking the executor or exposing the offending value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L10)).
+- Input that satisfies the declared schema reaches the executor unchanged, including properties not listed by the schema, and reaches it exactly once ([validated by: validates known fields and forwards valid input with an extra property unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L37)).
+- A static schema that cannot be compiled fails during registration with the tool name in the error, while a function-valued definition is validated against the schema it resolves for each execution ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and resolves function-valued schemas for each execution](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L66)).
